  "description": "Error messages made from API answers. A call (GET /api/endpoints/acme) answered with status and body (exactly these characters, as UTF-8) fails with an error whose text before any hint the SDK adds is expected.message: the body's string message, else its string error (a blank one, as JavaScript's trim() sees it, gives way), cut to 1000 characters with ... after it; a message that is only a code (lower-case ASCII letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter) becomes the status in words, alone when the code only names the status, else with the code in brackets; a body that is not a JSON object with either is kept as it came, cut to 200 characters. Characters are code points, so a cut never splits a surrogate pair. expected.hinted says whether the SDK adds its recovery hint, which only a 401 or 404 message under 30 characters (UTF-16 units) gets; the hint's wording is each SDK's own. On any status but 401, 404 and 429 (whose message is each SDK's rate-limit text) the error's message is expected.message itself. expected.code is the API's error code as the TypeScript SDK reads it: error when it is the body's first key and a code, else a code field that is a code, else null. A port lists in its test the vectors where it differs, and why.",
